WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.400
-Welcome back to the show.
It is so great to see you.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.200
-Oh! It's all been on Zoom,
and it's finally real.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.968
-It's real! You're really real!
-Oh, you're real!

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:08.167
-Oh, I'm so excited.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.501
I want to talk to you
about so many things.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:12.567
Last time, I think, we talked,
you were just engaged.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.200
-Yes.
-But now you're married.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.300
-Now I'm married.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.534
-Yeah, you did --
Buddy, congratulations.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:17.567
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:19.868
-I'm so happy for you.
-Thank you.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.901
-How was the wedding?
How was everything?

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.767
-It's -- He's backstage,
so it's going really well.

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:25.934
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.968
-He's here.
-Yeah. Was it as planned?

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.734
Everything went according to
plan with the wedding?

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.767
-Yeah, everything
went according to plan.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:34.133
And we were planning it
while shooting "Windfall."

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.267
So that was --
It was a lot on our plate.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.934
-I mean, I've been
seeing you everywhere,

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:39.300
because "Emily in Paris" --
You know I'm a fan.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.400
-Thank you.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.067
-So, that's when we
first had -- Yeah.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.000
-Thank you.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.200
-Let me just tell you something.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.767
It's one of the
top-five shows on Netflix --

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.701
in over 90 countries,
by the way.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.100
-Crazy.
-Isn't that wild?

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.534
-That's the magic of
Netflix, though.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.934
It's in so many countries
around the world, yeah,

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.701
and you're like, "I didn't even
know that they would be

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.801
interested in the show in,"
you know, X, Y, and Z.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:00:59.901
-It just got picked up for

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.501
a third and fourth season,
by the way.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:03.200
-Yeah. Thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.434
-Double whammy!
-We're so excited.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.701
We're so excited to come back.
-Well done.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:07.801
-Thank you.
-That's hard work on your part.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.000
-Thank you.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.467
-People are petitioning
online to have it --

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:13.901
Emily be in different cities.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.033
-I mean, honestly, I would go

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.601
all over the world with it,
if I could.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.033
But the one thing is like,
I just want to go to

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.801
streets where
you can wear flats,

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.868
because wearing heels -- I mean,

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:26.701
you wouldn't think how painful
that can be in Paris.

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.801
I actually literally went to
a podiatrist every week

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.667
to fix my feet because I was
wearing heels all the time --

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:33.734
-'Cause it's
cobblestone everywhere.

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:35.200
-Everywhere. Everywhere.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.267
And I had to have, like, insoles
made for every pair of shoes.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.300
-Oh, my gosh.
-I'm not kidding.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.634
-You're like, "Let's do a season

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.968
where Emily
just has to wear sneakers."

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:47.300
-Yeah, "Emily in Flats."
-Yeah, "Emily in Flats."

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.701
That's exactly right.
-Like, why not?

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.334
-Why not?
But everyone's getting into it.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.968
Everyone wants to get involved.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.400
I'm sure you saw Peyton Manning
on "Weekend Update" on

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.667
"Saturday Night Live"
a couple weeks ago.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.968
-That was crazy.
That was so absurd.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:04.200
When I saw -- My phone has never
blown up more.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.367
-How fun --
-It was so cool!

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.601
-He's one of the funniest,
nicest guys, too.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.534
-Is he?
-Oh, he's the greatest, yeah.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:13.767
And just goes with the thing and
sees where he can go with it.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.300
And I thought that was
perfect delivery.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.734
-But I just want to know,
like, is he a fan?

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.701
Like, is he really a fan?
-I think he is now.

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.367
-That's like --
I mean, he is now, yeah.

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:23.334
-Now he's part of the world.
Now he's into the world.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.667
-Now he's part of
the Emily universe.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.000
-Now he has to make a cameo.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.167
-By the way, I'm like,
"How can we make that happen?"

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.200
-Yeah, done. He's watching.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.667
-I mean, Peyton,
if you're watching...

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.767
-Yeah, let's take care of this.

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.801
I want to say,
you just had a huge weekend.

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:38.234
"Windfall"
just came out on Netflix.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:39.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
People have seen it already.

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.801
-Thank you.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.133
-When I watched it again,

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.234
it was the number-4 trending
movie on Netflix.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.133
I go, "Man, you're just owning
Netflix right now."

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.534
That's great, but --

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:49.534
-Very different than
"Emily," though.

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:50.934
-Very, very different.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:52.467
Ooh, it's creepy and good.
I loved the whole idea of it.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:53.767
-Thank you.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:57.100
-But for this one --
It was also released on Fri--

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.334
last Friday,
which was your birthday.

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:01.434
-It was, yeah.
And that was unplanned.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:02.434
-That's a birthday present
for you.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:03.501
-It was.

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:05.434
It was really special
birthday gift.

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:08.200
I actually just kept thinking of
it as, like, "Windfall" day.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.234
You have a birthday every year,
but "Windfall" is only one day.

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.868
You know, it only comes out
once a year.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.467
It was, like,
a very special day.

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.100
-Talk to me about "Windfall,"

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.901
because your
husband directed it, right?

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.267
-He did, yeah.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.834
-And you made this during --
Is it during the pandemic?

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.767
-During the pandemic, yeah.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.300
Charlie conceptualized it with

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.901
his three friends
and writing partners,

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:31.267
and they did it in one location
during the pandemic --

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:34.300
to not reference COVID itself,
but to reference the feeling of

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.467
feeling claustrophobic
and stuck in one's environment,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.934
'cause it does take place
in one location

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:42.534
with three, kind of four,
cast members.

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:45.834
And it was all done with
no shutdowns

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:48.667
at the height of the pandemic,
right before "Emily" Season 2.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:52.267
So it was a real, like,
team effort,

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:53.534
and we're really proud of it.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:56.501
-I mean, doing all that
and getting married --

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.067
-Oh, we were planning
the wedding and shooting

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:00.400
and going off to Paris.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.000
And it was a wild --
-That's bonding right there.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.934
-It was a wild --
It was -- And he's --

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.400
Like I said, he's backstage.
It all happened.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.767
-Going strong. Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:11.300
Who came up with
the idea for this --

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.367
-Well, Jason Segel
came up with the initial idea,

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:17.234
but Charlie,
Andrew Kevin Walker,

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.667
and Justin Lader,
Charlie's writing partner,

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.467
all conceptualized it
on Zoom over the pandemic.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:24.334
-It is good and scary
and creepy,

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:27.267
but can you explain
the plot for everyone?

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.334
-Yeah, the premise is
what happens when

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:34.534
a robbery goes wrong, I guess,
the realistic,

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.334
dark-comedic-thriller elements
of what happens when

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.667
a robbery goes wrong.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.934
And there's a guy that comes
into a vacation home of

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:44.267
a C.E.O. and his wife
and what ensues after that.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:46.634
-It's crazy and --
Yeah, of course,

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:48.267
and Jason Segel, of course.

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:49.467
He thought of some -- Yeah.

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.300
-And, I mean, Jesse Plemons.
-Jesse Plemons.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.167
-He can do no wrong.
-He really can't.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.934
-And he's, like,
freaking nominated for an Oscar.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.033
I mean, come on.
-Come on.

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.267
Yeah, give it up for
Jesse Plemons.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:58.400
-Yes.
-He is unbelievable.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.434
But every -- You are, too.
-Thank you.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:03.434
-Everybody is great, and it
goes -- twists and turns,

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:04.734
and next thing you know,
you're like,

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.934
"Oh, this is really weird
and it's cool and it's fun."

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:08.033
And then you go...
[ Gasps ]

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.200
Okay, now it's like" --

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.033
-I get to do some fun stuff.
-Yeah.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:13.601
No spoilers,
but, yeah, you really do.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:14.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:16.567
Here's Lily Collins in
"Windfall."

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:17.868
Take a look at this.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:20.734
-All three of us -- we have to
find a way through this.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:24.033
So it comes down to
how much and how soon.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.868
So, how much?

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:30.767
-To what?

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:32.300
To disappear
and start a new life?

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.467
It looks like that's what
it's going to take, so,

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:41.267
you know...$150,000.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.133
What?
-150,000?

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.667
-150,000.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.267
-You think that's enough?

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:49.567
-Yeah, I think you're probably
gonna want more than that.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:53.467
-If you are looking for
any reasonable quality of life,

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:54.601
yes, that's right.

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:55.901
-You know what?

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.100
Something tells me that maybe
you and I have some

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.734
very different pictures
of quality of life.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:02.634
-Yeah! Lily Collins!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:04.801
"Windfall" is
streaming now on Netflix.

